# UI plugins: `GM_UI_PLUGINS`, `GET /api/ui/plugins` and the plugin loader

## What to build

Give the commercial repository a small, build-independent way to add UI to graph-manager without forking: `GM_UI_PLUGINS` lists ES module URLs (absolute `https://` URLs or paths starting with `/`). After sign-in the UI reads `GET /api/ui/plugins` (behind login) and `import()`s each module. Each module default-exports `(api) => void`, where `api` is `{ React, registerNav({ label, path }), registerRoute({ path, element }), registerTopbar(element), registerSettingsSection({ title, element }) }`. graph-manager passes **its own** React module as `api.React`, so plugins never bundle a second copy (hooks work because there is one React). A plugin that fails to load is logged with `console.error` and skipped; with no plugins the UI is exactly as before. Plugins add to the router (`App.tsx`), the nav and the top of the nav (`Shell.tsx`) and the Settings page (`Settings.tsx`) **additively**: nothing that exists is removed or reordered.

Only `apps/graph-manager` changes. **`packages/graph-execution` must not change.** Plugin URLs are trusted configuration (like any other `GM_*` variable): no sandboxing, no integrity check. graph-manager does not serve the plugin files itself; a path starting with `/` is served by whatever sits in front of graph-manager (the commercial gateway).

### Already in the codebase (from the tasks this depends on)

The Workspaces tab is gone: no `/workspaces` page (it redirects to `/terminals`), no Workspaces nav item, no `g w` chord; the Terminals page has the New terminal dialog and sessions in its sidebar; Settings has a **Repositories** section (and an **Account** card from built-in accounts, an **Agents** section may exist). `/api/auth/me` returns `{ user, mode, … }`. Read the current `App.tsx`, `Shell.tsx` and `Settings.tsx` before editing — they changed since the original layout; keep everything they render.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.ts` — `Config`, `envSchema` (the `optional` helper), `loadConfig`; add `GM_UI_PLUGINS`. **Add, do not rewrite**: sibling tasks add their own variables to the same schema.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.test.ts` — config test style (`loadConfig({...})`, `toThrow(ConfigError)`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/health.ts` (9 lines) — the smallest route module; mirror it for `routes/ui.ts`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts` — `AppContext`, route registration list under `// feature routes (one line per feature)`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/auth.ts` `needsAuth` — every `/api/*` path needs a login, so `/api/ui/plugins` is behind login with no change.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/reviewers.test.ts` (lines 1–30) and `src/server/test-helpers.ts` (`appWithLogin(overrides)`, `testConfig`) — server test pattern.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/App.tsx` — the auth gate and `<Routes>`; plugin routes go before the `path="*"` catch-all.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.tsx` — `NavItem` (around lines 42–53), the `nav-brand` block and `nav-links` list (around lines 136–186), `nav-footer`. Plugin nav items go at the end of `nav-links`, after Settings; the top-bar slot goes right after the `nav-brand` block.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.css` — rail rules (lines ~77–93: `.gm-shell.rail …` and the `@media` block hiding labels below 1100 px); hide the plugin slot in the rail the same way.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Settings.tsx` — the page's sections; plugin sections go last, after Appearance.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/Icon.tsx` (line 3 `IconName`) — plugin nav items use the existing `"menu"` icon.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/App.test.tsx`, `Shell.test.tsx`, `Settings.test.tsx` — how they stub `fetch` and render; extend their fake APIs with `/api/ui/plugins` → `{ plugins: [] }` where they answer every URL.

## Patterns to follow

**Route module (mirror `routes/health.ts`):**
```ts
import type { FastifyInstance } from "fastify";
import type { AppContext } from "../app.js";
export async function uiRoutes(app: FastifyInstance, ctx: AppContext): Promise<void> {
  app.get("/api/ui/plugins", async () => ({ plugins: ctx.config.uiPlugins ?? [] }));
}
```

**Config errors:** `throw new ConfigError("…")` from `loadConfig` after the zod parse (see how other exact messages are thrown there).

**External store for React (`useSyncExternalStore`)**: an immutable snapshot object replaced on every change, a `Set` of listeners; `getSnapshot` must return the same object until something changes.

**Web tests:** `// @vitest-environment jsdom`, `vi.stubGlobal("fetch", vi.fn(async (url) => …))`, `render(<App />)`, `await screen.findByTestId(...)` (see `App.test.tsx` lines 1–35).

## Step-by-step tasks

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**: `Config.uiPlugins?: string[]`; `GM_UI_PLUGINS: optional` in `envSchema`; in `loadConfig`, split on `,`, trim, drop empty entries; each entry must be an absolute `https://` URL (`new URL(entry).protocol === "https:"`) or a path starting with `/` but not `//`; otherwise `throw new ConfigError(\`GM_UI_PLUGINS entries must be https:// URLs or paths starting with /: ${entry}\`)`. Set `config.uiPlugins` only when at least one entry remains.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-manager -- config`

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/ui.ts`; UPDATE `app.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**: `GET /api/ui/plugins` → `{ plugins: string[] }` (the configured list, `[]` when unset). Register with one line under `// feature routes`: `await uiRoutes(app, ctx);`.
- **GOTCHA**: no auth code needed: `needsAuth` already covers `/api/*` (401 without a login, also in gateway mode without an identity).
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-manager -- routes/ui`

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/plugins.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**:
  ```ts
  import * as React from "react";
  import { useSyncExternalStore, type ReactNode } from "react";
  import { api } from "./api";

  export interface PluginNav { label: string; path: string }
  export interface PluginRoute { path: string; element: ReactNode }
  export interface PluginSettingsSection { title: string; element: ReactNode }
  export interface PluginApi {
    React: typeof React;
    registerNav(item: PluginNav): void;
    registerRoute(route: PluginRoute): void;
    registerTopbar(element: ReactNode): void;
    registerSettingsSection(section: PluginSettingsSection): void;
  }
  export interface PluginRegistry { nav: PluginNav[]; routes: PluginRoute[]; topbar: ReactNode[]; settings: PluginSettingsSection[]; loaded: boolean }

  /** Imports one module URL. Replaced in tests (vitest cannot import http URLs). */
  export type Importer = (url: string) => Promise<{ default?: unknown }>;
  const defaultImporter: Importer = (url) => import(/* @vite-ignore */ url);

  export function usePlugins(): PluginRegistry;            // useSyncExternalStore(subscribe, snapshot)
  /** Reads /api/ui/plugins and imports each module once, in order. Never throws; marks `loaded` when done. */
  export async function loadPlugins(importer: Importer = defaultImporter): Promise<void>;
  /** Tests only: empties the registry and forgets that plugins were loaded. */
  export function resetPlugins(): void;
  ```
  - `loadPlugins` is idempotent (a second call returns the first call's promise). It fetches `api<{ plugins?: unknown }>("/api/ui/plugins")`; a failed request or a non-array → no plugins. For each URL: `const mod = await importer(url)`; `mod.default` must be a function, else `console.error(\`graph-manager: plugin ${url} has no default export function\`)`; call it with a `PluginApi` whose register functions validate input (nav/route `path` must start with `/`; labels/titles non-empty strings) and `console.error` + ignore bad input. Any throw from the import or the plugin → `console.error(\`graph-manager: plugin ${url} failed to load:\`, err)` and continue with the next. Each module is given its own api object; registrations made after `loadPlugins` resolved still show up (snapshot updates).
  - Every change replaces the snapshot object (`snapshot = { ...snapshot, nav: [...snapshot.nav, item] }`) and notifies listeners.
  - A plugin route whose path equals a built-in one (`/`, `/runs`, `/terminals`, `/projects`, `/reviewers`, `/settings`, `/runs/:ws/:runId`, and the logged-out pages) is ignored with `console.error` — plugins add, never replace.
- **GOTCHA**: keep `/* @vite-ignore */` so Vite leaves the dynamic import alone in the production build. Plugins are loaded only after sign-in (`/api/ui/plugins` needs a login).
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/App.tsx`

- **IMPLEMENT**: when the auth state becomes `in`, call `void loadPlugins()` once. Inside the existing `<Routes>`, add `{plugins.routes.map((r) => <Route key={r.path} path={r.path} element={r.element} />)}` **before** the `path="*"` route (keep every existing route). Make the catch-all wait for plugins: while `!plugins.loaded`, the `*` route renders the existing loading gate (`<div className="gate" role="status" …>`), so a deep link such as `/billing` is not redirected to `/runs` before the plugin that owns it registered; once loaded, the catch-all redirects to `/runs` as today. Add a safety timeout: `loadPlugins` marks `loaded` after 10 s even if an import hangs (the late plugin can still register).
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-manager -- App`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.tsx` and `Shell.css`

- **IMPLEMENT**: `const plugins = usePlugins();`. At the end of `nav-links` (after the Settings `NavItem`): `{plugins.nav.map((n) => <NavItem key={n.path} to={n.path} icon="menu" label={n.label} />)}`. Right after the `nav-brand` block: when `plugins.topbar.length > 0`, `<div className="nav-plugin-slot" data-testid="nav-plugin-slot">{plugins.topbar.map((el, i) => <Fragment key={i}>{el}</Fragment>)}</div>`. CSS: `.nav-plugin-slot { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; padding: 0 6px; }`, hidden in the rail (`.gm-shell.rail .nav-plugin-slot` and the below-1100 px media block, alongside the existing hidden selectors).
- **GOTCHA**: do not change the order or labels of the existing nav items (tests assert them); with no plugins the DOM is identical to before.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-manager -- Shell`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Settings.tsx`

- **IMPLEMENT**: after the last existing section (Appearance), render `plugins.settings.map((s) => <section key={s.title} className="settings-card" aria-label={s.title} data-testid="plugin-settings-section"><h2>{s.title}</h2>{s.element}</section>)`.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-manager -- Settings`

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/test-fixtures/hello-plugin.js` (the test plugin)

- **IMPLEMENT** a plain ES module written the way a real plugin is (no imports, React only from `api`):
  ```js
  // A UI plugin as GM_UI_PLUGINS loads it: React comes from graph-manager through `api`.
  export default function hello(api) {
    const h = api.React.createElement;
    function Billing() {
      const [n, setN] = api.React.useState(0); // hooks work: one React
      return h("section", { "data-testid": "page-billing" }, h("h1", null, "Billing"), h("button", { type: "button", onClick: () => setN(n + 1) }, `Clicked ${n}`));
    }
    api.registerNav({ label: "Billing", path: "/billing" });
    api.registerRoute({ path: "/billing", element: h(Billing) });
    api.registerTopbar(h("span", { "data-testid": "plan-badge" }, "Pro plan"));
    api.registerSettingsSection({ title: "Plan", element: h("p", null, "You are on the Pro plan.") });
  }
  ```
  It must pass `npm run lint` (the root ESLint config lints `.js` files with `js.configs.recommended`; it uses no globals). It is not imported by the app, so Vite does not bundle it.

### Tests

- **CREATE `src/server/routes/ui.test.ts`**: with `appWithLogin({ uiPlugins: ["/plugins/hello.js", "https://cdn.example.com/p.js"] })`, `GET /api/ui/plugins` → 200 `{ plugins: [...] }`; without a cookie → 401; with no `uiPlugins` → `{ plugins: [] }`.
- **UPDATE `src/server/config.test.ts`**: `GM_UI_PLUGINS="/plugins/a.js, https://x.example.com/b.js"` → two trimmed entries; unset/blank → `uiPlugins` undefined; `http://x/a.js`, `plugins/a.js` and `//evil/a.js` → ConfigError with the exact message.
- **CREATE `src/web/plugins.test.tsx`** (jsdom; call `resetPlugins()` in `afterEach`):
  - The test plugin end to end: stub `fetch` so `/api/auth/me` → `{ user: { id: "admin", name: "admin" }, mode: "users" }`, `/api/ui/plugins` → `{ plugins: ["/plugins/hello.js"] }`, every other URL → a harmless `{}`-ish answer like the other App tests. Make the importer serve the fixture: render `<App />` after calling `loadPlugins((url) => url === "/plugins/hello.js" ? import("./test-fixtures/hello-plugin.js") : Promise.reject(new Error("unknown")))` (App's own later `loadPlugins()` call returns the same promise, so the injected importer wins). Assert: a nav link "Billing" appears after Settings; clicking it shows `page-billing`, and its button counts clicks (proves `api.React` hooks work); `plan-badge` is in `nav-plugin-slot`; Settings shows a `plugin-settings-section` titled "Plan"; a deep link `window.history.pushState({}, "", "/billing")` before render lands on `page-billing`, not `/runs`.
  - A failing plugin is skipped: importer rejects for `/bad.js` and resolves the fixture for `/plugins/hello.js` (list `["/bad.js", "/plugins/hello.js"]`) → `console.error` called once with a message containing `/bad.js`, and Billing still appears. A module whose default is not a function is skipped the same way.
  - No plugins: `/api/ui/plugins` → `{ plugins: [] }` → the nav links are exactly the built-in ones and there is no `nav-plugin-slot` or `plugin-settings-section`; `/api/ui/plugins` failing (500) behaves the same.
  - A plugin route on `/settings` is ignored (the built-in Settings page still shows).
- **UPDATE** `App.test.tsx`, `Shell.test.tsx`, `Settings.test.tsx` only as needed so their fetch fakes answer `/api/ui/plugins` and their existing assertions still hold.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `GM_UI_PLUGINS` accepts a comma-separated list of `https://` URLs and `/`-paths; anything else stops startup with `GM_UI_PLUGINS entries must be https:// URLs or paths starting with /: <entry>`.
- [ ] `GET /api/ui/plugins` → `{ "plugins": [...] }` behind login (401 without).
- [ ] A plugin's `registerNav`, `registerRoute`, `registerTopbar` and `registerSettingsSection` add a nav item, a page (also reachable by a deep link), an item at the top of the nav and a Settings section; the plugin uses graph-manager's React via `api.React`, and hooks work.
- [ ] A plugin that fails to import or throws is logged with `console.error` and skipped; other plugins still load.
- [ ] With no plugins the UI is unchanged (same nav items, same pages, no extra elements).
- [ ] `packages/graph-execution` unchanged.
- [ ] Tests pass: `npm test -w graph-manager -- plugins routes/ui config App Shell Settings`

## Validation commands

```bash
# Type / lint
npm run typecheck && npm run lint

# Tests for this slice
npm test -w graph-manager -- plugins routes/ui config App Shell Settings

# Whole graph-manager suite
npm test -w graph-manager

# The engine package must not change
git diff --stat -- packages/graph-execution
```
